WEBVTT

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:08.170
Mind Trance System.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:11.300
In the same way the Miguel
Jump uses Orichalt

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:13.580
to traverse through a different
plane of existence,

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:20.330
the Mind Trance System takes
someone's consciousness data

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:23.640
and transfers it to the I-machine's archive.

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:27.000
The responses of an I-machine linked
with the human consciousness

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:29.660
are no different from that of
a flesh and blood body.

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:33.580
Moreover, it allows for the execution of precise
jobs better than an ordinary human body

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:36.980
due to the superior supervisory capabilities.

00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:41.180
Naturally, the consciousness data
can be returned back to the body.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:44.460
Because a back-up is made in advance,

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:46.400
in the case the I-machine is lost

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.850
there is no possibility of losing data.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:52.320
The only thing lost will be the short
memories of conducting the work.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:55.170
And the feeling of fear at that time.

00:00:56.290 --> 00:01:02.680
Installation of this system will decrease personnel
loss rate to 0.03% of the current rate.

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:07.300
Moreover, the lack of necessity to equip
them with life support systems

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:11.380
allows us to expect a decrease of more
than 30% in production costs.

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:14.040
That's enough talk.

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:16.260
Allow me to demonstrate.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:26.090
This machine hosts the consciousness data of the
Kain Arisugawa that has been talking to you.

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:30.500
This technology is one you could call necessary
for an age of space exploration.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:33.380
The Mind Trance System.

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:39.130
Thank you very much.

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:43.170
Although our normal body is the
one mankind is most used to,

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:44.820
I think...

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:54.250
A daydream...

00:01:57.130 --> 00:02:02.290
Or a remainder of those hateful memories?

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:47.980
Papa, I got the news from eight hours ago.

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:49.630
Well let's hear them, Clair.

00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:50.760
Let's see,

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:56.360
An astrogeology professor at the Planet Federation
academy and an authority in the field of astrogeology,

00:03:56.360 --> 00:04:02.640
Attomy Kinsberg, was accused of illegally providing
observation data on a resource asteroid

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:07.690
obtained under academy protection to a large-scale
construction company, the Fujima Corporation.

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:12.030
Professor Attomy has declared that the one illegally
providing information was one of his seminar students,

00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:14.240
Mikuri Maya.

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:15.800
It wasn't me!

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:17.240
We get it.

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:20.620
That bastard just shifted the blame to you.

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:22.370
Shifted the blame?

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:28.630
The suspect Mikuri Maya's whereabouts are unknown
since the mining accident at the Omega 3 asteroid.

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:30.260
Chances of survival are said to be slim.

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:31.210
No they're not!

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:36.980
So basically the Prof was afraid of getting
busted and tried to kill you off.

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:43.050
You should be really grateful to our Fa-Loser who
picked your body up while you were drifting about.

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:44.860
Of course I'm grateful.

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:50.190
But to prove my innocence I really have to
return to the academy as fast as possible!

00:04:50.190 --> 00:04:51.780
They'll detain you as soon as you get there.

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:52.130
But I'm innocent!
They'll detain you as soon as you get there.

00:04:52.130 --> 00:04:53.070
But I'm innocent!

00:04:53.070 --> 00:04:57.310
They'll just drive you into a
corner with their authority.

00:04:57.310 --> 00:05:01.500
Even if you take it to the court, they'll
win through the power of money.

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:05.710
You'll get arrested, sent to prison and your
life will go on a downwards spiral.

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:06.500
No way...

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:07.980
Guess there's no choice.

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:10.420
Should I break the good news to you, girlie?

00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:14.300
Our Orichalt-specialized mining
company, Escavate,

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:17.400
is currently hiring personnel
knowledgeable in astrogeology.

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:21.350
Maya, you were top of the class
in the astrogeology department, right?

00:05:21.350 --> 00:05:22.770
Now that's great!

00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:25.170
Alright, usually I'd take you
in as a part timer,

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:27.760
but as an exception you'll be
hired as a full-time employee.

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:29.210
What wonderful terms!

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:32.930
Wait, was I your target all along?

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:36.650
You knew about the professor's evil plan
but still pretended not to notice...

00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:38.880
We're not that evil, you know.

00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:44.700
Although, I guess we wouldn't have bothered rescuing
you if we didn't know you're good at astrogeology.

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:47.010
I can't believe this.

00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:49.610
Are you demons?

00:05:50.730 --> 00:05:52.880
If you've got problems, get out right now.

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:57.170
People who can't use I-machines
properly have no place here.

00:05:57.170 --> 00:05:58.900
Ido, that was too much.

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:00.450
Peace, peace.

00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:02.640
I was going to leave even
without you saying that!

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:04.140
Yes, I'll leave right away!

00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:05.460
And how?

00:06:06.210 --> 00:06:07.810
By floating all the way back?

00:06:08.690 --> 00:06:12.370
Or you could work with us until you
save up enough to pay for your ride.

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:16.650
I'm looking forward to working with you.

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:41.880
It looks like an object possessing a resource
ratio of 2.0 has made a spatial jump.

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:46.890
It's a rogue planet releasing the strongest
Miguel Storm we've ever observed.

00:06:46.890 --> 00:06:51.010
Since the level of the storm and the
amount of Orichalt are proportional.

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:52.940
I've got some high hopes for it.

00:06:53.370 --> 00:06:58.930
We'll designate info about this object as top
secret and conduct cover mining on it.

00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:01.500
Will that be acceptable?

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:06.680
How about deploying the
military just to be safe?

00:07:07.540 --> 00:07:10.440
I said "I'm looking forward
to working with you."

00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:12.440
Yeah, I said that.

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:15.330
But why am I supposed to
do something like this?

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:19.450
Shouldn't an interstellar ship of this class
have its maintenance done by pros?

00:07:19.490 --> 00:07:21.260
It's to make sure you've got guts.

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:26.160
Our boss is ex-military, so he can't
just lose that character.

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:28.640
What an outdated way of thinking...

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:30.140
Oh right, your name?

00:07:30.140 --> 00:07:31.370
Rick Ayer.

00:07:31.370 --> 00:07:32.420
Just Rick is fine.

00:07:32.420 --> 00:07:33.940
I'm Mikuri Maya.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:37.040
I'll be in your care just for a short while,

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:39.650
because I'm leaving as soon
as I gather the money.

00:07:39.690 --> 00:07:41.450
Is what Ido said

00:07:41.450 --> 00:07:43.020
still bothering you?

00:07:43.180 --> 00:07:46.040
He was just looking out for
you in his own way.

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:49.620
Orichalt mining is a job you stake
your life on, after all.

00:07:49.850 --> 00:07:53.660
He wanted to say that you can't
do it with half-baked resolve.

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:56.060
Staking your life sounds like
a bit of an overstatement.

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:58.440
We conduct work in I-machines anyway.

00:07:58.440 --> 00:08:02.260
Even if you lose the machine,
you can just Mind Reload.

00:08:02.260 --> 00:08:03.770
You don't die.

00:08:03.770 --> 00:08:06.160
Well I guess that's how it is normally...

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:10.220
Rick, did you really take out an I-machine
just to talk to me here?

00:08:10.450 --> 00:08:15.040
It's a waste of energy, you really
should just Mind Out already.

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:17.580
Now that's new.

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:20.090
How many years has it been
since I was last told that?

00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:23.100
Big bro here has taken a liking to you.

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:26.250
What is it with him?

00:08:26.930 --> 00:08:29.890
What Orichalt- mining company?

00:08:29.890 --> 00:08:31.840
They're just a bunch of gangsters!

00:08:31.970 --> 00:08:34.700
I might go with the flow easily,

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:37.960
but that doesn't mean I'll be
stuck working here forever!

00:08:37.960 --> 00:08:39.040
I'll get out of here!

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:41.140
I'll get out of here for sure!

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:48.000
Zephyr, have you got any valuable info?

00:08:48.100 --> 00:08:49.720
For Escavate?

00:08:49.770 --> 00:08:50.720
I've got some.

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:51.560
Right here.

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:52.650
I'll buy it.

00:08:52.650 --> 00:08:53.680
Is 3,000 okay?

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:57.620
If you'd go on a date with
me in your human body,

00:08:57.620 --> 00:08:59.230
I don't mind giving to you for free.

00:08:59.230 --> 00:09:00.810
I'll send 5,000 your way.

00:09:02.280 --> 00:09:03.410
Thanks for your patronage!

00:09:03.410 --> 00:09:05.120
I'll send the data right away.

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:07.750
A new planet?

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:08.640
How is it?

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:09.810
Up to your liking?

00:09:09.810 --> 00:09:11.450
Yes, quite.

00:09:15.340 --> 00:09:17.120
Maya? It's Clair.

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:19.720
Are you satisfied with your room?

00:09:19.720 --> 00:09:23.170
I'm sorry it's so soon after you just rested,
but the briefing will be happening soon.

00:09:23.170 --> 00:09:25.570
Could you come to the expanded space?

00:09:25.570 --> 00:09:27.360
The expanded space?

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:29.140
Can't we just meet up in person?

00:09:29.140 --> 00:09:30.260
Please be there.

00:09:32.060 --> 00:09:35.100
When in Rome, do as the Romans do, huh?

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:53.120
Maya!

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:53.970
Welcome!

00:09:53.970 --> 00:09:54.620
Oh?

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:57.120
No problem getting here, huh?

00:09:57.120 --> 00:09:59.740
Um, who might you be?

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:00.890
The president!

00:10:00.890 --> 00:10:01.690
My dad.

00:10:01.690 --> 00:10:04.210
Ah, so that's what you look like.

00:10:04.210 --> 00:10:07.410
Rick... Has arrived!

00:10:08.590 --> 00:10:10.720
The I-Machine is your avatar, too?

00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:13.100
Of course! This is me after all.

00:10:22.840 --> 00:10:25.330
Looks like everyone's here.

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:27.660
Karla? So pretty...

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:28.880
You think?

00:10:30.610 --> 00:10:31.820
Thank you.

00:10:31.820 --> 00:10:33.860
Karla, your report.

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:35.290
Who's the sponsor?

00:10:35.450 --> 00:10:37.040
It's "Planet Work."

00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:42.500
A mining company financed with
the Federation's public funds.

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:44.160
Very well financed, too.

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:48.280
Seems like this famous company
obtained a right to mine Orichalt

00:10:48.280 --> 00:10:50.410
and it's looking for an excavation
subcontractor.

00:10:50.730 --> 00:10:55.760
Whether the excavation succeeds or fails,
the reward is 10 million.

00:10:55.760 --> 00:10:58.810
10 million?! Those conditions
sound great, right?

00:10:58.810 --> 00:11:00.900
That's an extra zero over the usual amount.

00:11:00.900 --> 00:11:02.980
Karla. There must be a catch?

00:11:02.980 --> 00:11:04.020
Of course.

00:11:04.020 --> 00:11:08.140
After all, the mining target is
a newly discovered object

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:11.650
in the planetary system of Vega of the Lyra
constellation with the diameter of 20,000 km.

00:11:11.650 --> 00:11:12.990
A new planet?

00:11:12.990 --> 00:11:15.370
Why did nobody find it until now?

00:11:15.370 --> 00:11:19.410
Going by Federation Standard Time, looks
like it suddenly manifested two days ago.

00:11:19.410 --> 00:11:20.880
Miguel Jump?

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:23.580
It's possible.

00:11:23.980 --> 00:11:25.660
A storm in the planet's atmosphere...

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:30.970
Even going by the remote scan data it's stronger
than Level 5, the highest observed category.

00:11:30.970 --> 00:11:37.970
If there's enough Orichalt there to cause such a storm,
a planetary-scale warp is not out of the question.

00:11:37.970 --> 00:11:41.660
The data about this new planet is full
of "unknown" and "unconfirmed."

00:11:41.660 --> 00:11:42.980
What's going on?

00:11:42.980 --> 00:11:45.310
It was discovered just two days ago.

00:11:45.310 --> 00:11:48.220
And they're saying to dig that?
That's ridiculous.

00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:50.070
That's why it's 10 million.

00:11:50.070 --> 00:11:52.010
It's way too risky.

00:11:52.010 --> 00:11:54.860
But Ido won't refuse, right?

00:11:56.700 --> 00:11:58.450
What do you say, Ido?

00:11:59.700 --> 00:12:01.070
This job...

00:12:01.610 --> 00:12:02.790
I accept it.

00:12:10.230 --> 00:12:15.320
Mmm! To take up a job with this
little info, that's our Ido.

00:12:15.320 --> 00:12:16.930
You're even crazier than me.

00:12:16.930 --> 00:12:18.430
It's too dangerous.

00:12:18.430 --> 00:12:22.480
In the first place, how are we going to
pass a storm stronger than level 5?

00:12:22.480 --> 00:12:23.690
There's a way.

00:12:23.690 --> 00:12:25.460
You couldn't mean...

00:12:27.700 --> 00:12:29.750
You get it?

00:12:33.890 --> 00:12:36.380
Proceeding with the Miguel Jump sequence.

00:12:36.380 --> 00:12:37.920
Ido, what were you talking about?

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:40.300
Can you explain it to the rest of us?

00:12:40.300 --> 00:12:42.180
Target star: Vega in the constellation of Lyra.

00:12:42.180 --> 00:12:43.630
Deploying spatial mesh.

00:12:43.630 --> 00:12:45.180
Unit of measurement: AU.

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:46.820
Putting this ship in grid 1.

00:12:46.820 --> 00:12:49.230
Deploying grid 2 in the same space.

00:12:49.230 --> 00:12:54.550
The new planet has two satellites with the
diameters of 1,000 and 4,000 kilometers.

00:12:54.550 --> 00:12:56.680
Hmm, and?

00:12:56.680 --> 00:13:01.320
Because of their tidal force, there will be
periodic changes in geological activity.

00:13:01.470 --> 00:13:05.860
And because of that there will be gaps
in the Miguel Storm from time to time.

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:09.470
Time until Orichalt is released
from containment mechanism:

00:13:11.260 --> 00:13:17.690
But you won't know the state of the planetary surface when you arrive!

00:13:17.690 --> 00:13:19.780
We'll observe it while heading to the site.

00:13:19.780 --> 00:13:23.880
Ido, even for you excavating and surveying at the same time will be impossible.

00:13:23.960 --> 00:13:27.960
Well, we've got no choice but to send a surveying expert to back him up then.

00:13:28.590 --> 00:13:30.350
Wait, you mean?

00:13:31.820 --> 00:13:32.880
Orichalt, release.

00:13:32.980 --> 00:13:36.240
Is that why I'm in an I-machine too?

00:13:36.900 --> 00:13:38.380
Commencing Miguel Jump.

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:42.790
Arrival at the Miguel Line.

00:13:43.120 --> 00:13:45.510
Am I really going there?

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:48.360
You just have to report surveying data.

00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:50.270
After that it's Ido's job.

00:13:50.270 --> 00:13:51.440
But...

00:13:51.440 --> 00:13:53.110
If you're scared, you can stay.

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:55.180
Wait a bit!

00:14:01.560 --> 00:14:02.780
We're going there to work.

00:14:02.780 --> 00:14:03.520
Got that?

00:14:03.520 --> 00:14:04.910
Y-yes.

00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:07.790
Miguel Out.

00:14:11.340 --> 00:14:13.720
The asteroid situation is worse than I thought.

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:16.760
Even though I set it to a relatively safe location...

00:14:22.660 --> 00:14:23.790
Is the office okay?

00:14:23.870 --> 00:14:24.860
Negligible damage.

00:14:24.980 --> 00:14:26.860
We'll have to do some maintenance later.

00:14:27.110 --> 00:14:28.390
Send this thing out!

00:14:28.390 --> 00:14:29.820
In these conditions?

00:14:29.960 --> 00:14:33.060
The satellite influence will cause a storm here soon.

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:33.990
This is our chance.

00:14:34.120 --> 00:14:35.070
Alright.

00:14:35.270 --> 00:14:38.550
Launch it, and afterwards we'll
retreat to a safe distance.

00:14:38.550 --> 00:14:40.580
Throwing the Mattsun!

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:46.260
We're going to collide!

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:49.390
Stop it!

00:14:50.790 --> 00:14:53.080
Commencing excavation as
soon as we hit the surface.

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:54.430
There's a gravity anomaly!

00:14:54.430 --> 00:14:57.280
Mr. Ido, with these numbers,
the inside must be hollowed out!

00:14:57.280 --> 00:14:58.590
A hollow planet?

00:14:58.590 --> 00:15:00.350
We won't be able to set the drill up!

00:15:00.350 --> 00:15:02.670
Please withdraw from the landing orbit!

00:15:03.110 --> 00:15:04.150
There's a downburst.

00:15:04.150 --> 00:15:05.550
Must be the tidal power influence.

00:15:05.550 --> 00:15:06.840
No way!

00:15:08.700 --> 00:15:11.660
Temporarily shut down all sensory
systems other than hearing.

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:13.740
Reverse thrust!

00:15:26.040 --> 00:15:28.340
Retreat to a safe distance, complete.

00:15:28.560 --> 00:15:29.920
How's Ido and the girl?

00:15:30.040 --> 00:15:32.680
Because of the storm the
comms link is unstable.

00:15:32.720 --> 00:15:33.550
Goddammit.

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:37.350
I'll be waiting for them right on the
border of the rendezvous zone.

00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:41.040
You worried about them too?

00:15:42.740 --> 00:15:43.740
So am I.

00:15:53.780 --> 00:15:54.960
The drill...

00:15:55.110 --> 00:15:56.150
What do we do now?

00:15:56.260 --> 00:15:57.340
If it's like this...

00:15:59.740 --> 00:16:01.880
Mr. Ido! Where are you going?

00:16:02.100 --> 00:16:03.960
There's only one thing I have to do.

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:05.480
Wait!

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:07.480
Wait for me, please!

00:16:09.820 --> 00:16:12.340
This mesh-like pattern of cracks...

00:16:12.340 --> 00:16:14.340
The storm probably exits
through these tunnels.

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:15.440
Looks like it.

00:16:15.630 --> 00:16:19.840
Judging by the satellite orbit, the time the
storm subsides for is around 7 minutes.

00:16:19.920 --> 00:16:25.270
Based on vibration measurement, the shortest distance
to the storm occurrence site is 1,0000 meters.

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:29.630
Here's the fissure structure map based
on vibration and electric scans.

00:16:29.920 --> 00:16:31.600
Matches up with my prediction.

00:16:31.820 --> 00:16:32.200
Um?

00:16:38.470 --> 00:16:40.990
Mr. Ido, were you in astrogeology as well?

00:16:40.990 --> 00:16:42.310
I'm self-taught.

00:16:42.510 --> 00:16:45.020
I had plenty of time for thinking, after all.

00:16:45.220 --> 00:16:47.620
What do you mean?

00:16:49.080 --> 00:16:50.060
The storm?

00:16:50.500 --> 00:16:52.340
It's coming from above.

00:16:58.700 --> 00:17:04.300
Mr. Ido!

00:17:05.160 --> 00:17:06.380
I can hear you.

00:17:06.660 --> 00:17:08.240
You don't have to shout.

00:17:08.310 --> 00:17:09.960
This is awful.

00:17:10.060 --> 00:17:13.160
Mr. Ido, you can't do mining in this condition!

00:17:13.340 --> 00:17:15.820
Let's leave the machines here and Mind Out!

00:17:16.040 --> 00:17:17.080
Say what?

00:17:17.220 --> 00:17:21.040
I'm saying, let's leave the I-machines here and transfer
our consciousness data back to our bodies!

00:17:21.040 --> 00:17:22.790
I can't do that.

00:17:22.820 --> 00:17:24.030
Why?

00:17:24.350 --> 00:17:26.910
I don't have a body to return to.

00:17:28.040 --> 00:17:29.270
I'm an Evertrancer.

00:17:29.870 --> 00:17:31.560
Evertrancer...

00:17:32.140 --> 00:17:36.760
You abandoned your body and completely
uploaded your mind to the I-machine?

00:17:37.430 --> 00:17:41.190
That means if this machine is broken,
your consciousness data will...

00:17:44.430 --> 00:17:46.550
You shouldn't have covered me!

00:17:47.140 --> 00:17:49.360
I won't die even if the machine is lost!

00:17:49.360 --> 00:17:50.860
But despite that, why did you...

00:17:50.940 --> 00:17:55.700
Maybe I was quite a softy back when
I still had a flesh and blood body.

00:17:57.060 --> 00:17:58.270
I've got a proposition.

00:17:58.990 --> 00:18:00.670
You should Mind Out.

00:18:03.400 --> 00:18:06.400
Using the rest of your parts, I'll...

00:18:06.550 --> 00:18:08.560
Are you planning to look for the Orichalt?

00:18:08.830 --> 00:18:10.390
And if I say I am?

00:18:14.180 --> 00:18:15.950
I'm a coward.

00:18:16.420 --> 00:18:19.750
I can't do something like
abandoning a dying person.

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:21.600
It'll keep me up at night.

00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:28.380
If you equip my memory archive,
we can operate in data sharing mode.

00:18:32.310 --> 00:18:34.230
Please leave the navigation to me.

00:18:34.230 --> 00:18:36.110
I have to listen to an amateur's instructions?

00:18:36.110 --> 00:18:38.520
Dead ahead, a level 1 storm!

00:18:42.920 --> 00:18:44.640
Go directly downwards from here.

00:18:44.640 --> 00:18:45.600
Downwards?

00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:46.190
Yes.

00:18:46.190 --> 00:18:47.860
If my guess is right, there should be...

00:18:52.470 --> 00:18:54.340
Jump over the next chasm!

00:18:58.150 --> 00:18:59.480
There's a storm right behind me.

00:18:59.480 --> 00:19:01.000
Estimating it to be level 3.

00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:02.070
Your body can handle it.

00:19:02.070 --> 00:19:03.230
Let it push us!

00:19:03.230 --> 00:19:04.180
Don't ask for the impossible!

00:19:04.180 --> 00:19:06.180
It's a straight line for the Orichalt deposit!

00:19:06.180 --> 00:19:07.200
Let's go for it!

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:09.460
You've got more guts than I expected.

00:19:12.040 --> 00:19:12.830
A dead end!

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:13.640
Break through it!

00:19:13.640 --> 00:19:16.260
I guess ordering people around is the
one thing you're good for, huh?!

00:19:30.900 --> 00:19:32.560
T-This is...

00:19:32.760 --> 00:19:35.420
This size... This radiance...

00:19:35.630 --> 00:19:39.390
I've never seen this kind of Orichalt before.

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:41.860
How much time do we have
until the storm resumes?

00:19:42.300 --> 00:19:44.320
I expect around 2-3 minutes.

00:19:44.460 --> 00:19:45.820
I'm retrieving it.

00:19:47.630 --> 00:19:48.620
What is this?

00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:51.140
There's strong interference with
the consciousness signal!

00:19:51.190 --> 00:19:53.020
What about the effect on the archive...

00:19:55.160 --> 00:19:56.360
What's...

00:19:56.870 --> 00:19:58.830
What is this?

00:20:00.060 --> 00:20:01.860
What?

00:20:24.920 --> 00:20:26.260
It started!

00:20:26.350 --> 00:20:27.720
Rick, get back!

00:20:27.780 --> 00:20:29.820
The storm in reaction is
of the strongest class!

00:20:29.820 --> 00:20:31.920
Are you telling me to ditch them?

00:20:31.920 --> 00:20:34.070
At this rate you'll get hit by it too!

00:20:34.430 --> 00:20:35.760
Shit!

00:20:47.320 --> 00:20:48.220
Huh?

00:20:49.960 --> 00:20:51.750
Oh shit, seriously?

00:20:53.310 --> 00:20:55.840
Mr. Ido, that was too crazy!

00:20:55.920 --> 00:20:57.380
What are you saying now?

00:20:57.510 --> 00:20:59.280
This was your idea in the first place.

00:20:59.280 --> 00:21:01.420
We're talking about different scales here!

00:21:01.420 --> 00:21:03.300
You guys are insane!

00:21:04.990 --> 00:21:05.920
Hey, you.

00:21:05.920 --> 00:21:07.110
Uh, yes?

00:21:07.480 --> 00:21:08.670
Maya, was it?

00:21:09.500 --> 00:21:10.310
Good job.

00:21:10.550 --> 00:21:12.990
Y-You're welcome.

00:22:58.700 --> 00:23:00.400
How's the Orichalt?

00:23:00.400 --> 00:23:01.160
Huh?

00:23:08.790 --> 00:23:11.750
Wh-Who's that girl?

00:23:26.130 --> 00:23:32.400
The one who came out of the Orichalt's brilliance
shakes my very existence and presses the question:

00:23:32.400 --> 00:23:36.070
what worth is in a wanderer without a body?

00:23:36.070 --> 00:23:39.650
Below the armor, there's only chaos.
